      "descripcion": "Satellite imagery indicates that a low-pressure system located a few hundred miles south-southwest of the Gulf of Tehuantepec is producing a large area of showers and thunderstorms. This activity continues to become better organized, and if current trends persist, a tropical depression is expected to form later today. The system is expected to move westward to west-northwestward at around 10 mph during the next few days, well offshore the coast of southern Mexico. For additional information, including Gale Warnings, see the High Seas Forecast issued by the National Weather Service.",
